{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkCc2H7FyMvMEQYnCWX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm not aware of an official, dedicated CLI chat client for Cloudflare Agents. There are a few practical ways to talk to one from a terminal:\n\n- **`AgentClient` from the `agents` SDK** (`import { AgentClient } from \"agents/client\"`) works in Node, not just the browser. You can write a short readline loop that sends messages and prints responses.\n- **A raw WebSocket tool** like `wscat` or `websocat` can connect directly to the agent's endpoint, which is usually `wss://<your-worker>/agents/<agent-class-kebab>/<instance-name>`. You'd then send JSON matching your agent's message format.\n- **`curl`** works if your agent handles HTTP requests through `onRequest`.\n- **The MCP Inspector** (`npx @modelcontextprotocol/inspector`) is an option if your agent is an MCP server built with `McpAgent`.\n\nCloudflare's docs or the `cloudflare/agents` GitHub repo may have added a dedicated tool more recently, so check there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2246,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2246},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3157900e-80bb-4e2b-815c-78690a6d8fa9","uuid":"e5180866-4c5c-4eec-888b-0350ba64fcbe","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:09:58.869Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkCbQ4pf1G5bHcBpBSE"}
